  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nA strengthening low level jet will overspread our area through this \nmorning ahead of an approaching mid level short wave. Good moisture\nadvection associated with this will lead to developing shower\nactivity through the morning hours. Shower activity will then \ncontinue into this afternoon before beginning to taper off from west\nto east late this afternoon into this evening. Instability will \nremain weak at best, so think any embedded thunderstorm activity \nshould be fairly limited. PWs will creep up into the 1.5 inch range,\nso some of the stronger showers/storms will be capable of producing \nlocally heavy rainfall. However, given the overall dry antecedent \nconditions, any flooding concerns should be limited. \n\nKey message 2) \nA mid level short wave will drop down across the Great Lakes region \nand through the upper Ohio Valley Friday into Saturday. This will \nbring a chance of showers Friday into Friday night. This will also \nusher in a somewhat cooler airmass heading into the weekend. Daytime\nhighs will only be in the 50s Saturday and Sunday. Temperatures will\nthen gradually rebound Monday into Tuesday.",
